model c3_on_window
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.3 (#247, ruling 13, C12 (b)): `window(e1, e2)` stays an expression; written in a move's `on` it makes a hole day named by its movement (no cell holds it), as a window in a row does (L §4.4, §5.14). A plain movement at another place keeps its values. Written at C2, stored at the third pin."
source s "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place other: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input d0: date
input dx: date
input n4: int
move pw: transfers
  on window(d0, add_days(d0, n4))
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
move px: transfers
  on dx
  leg cash from world to other amount amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d0 = 2026-03-02 "s"
  dx = 2026-03-04 "s"
  n4 = 4 "s"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[other] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
ask before: bal(konto, 2026-03-01)
ask inside: bal(konto, 2026-03-04)
ask after: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask amount: pw.cash.amount
ask plain: bal(other, 2026-03-31)
ask n: count(m in transfers over 2026-03)
